-- Passage wg8-informative-writing-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('cebac371-d25d-53f5-b352-64c69ef72ab0', 'wg8-informative-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Life in a Tide Pool$q$, $q$(1) Twice a day, the ocean along rocky coasts pulls back during low tide. (2) When it does, small pools of seawater are left behind in the hollows of the rocks. (3) These are called tide pools. (4) Animals that live in tide pools must survive constant change. (5) At high tide, waves crash over them, and at low tide, the sun warms the water and some of it evaporates.

(6) Each tide pool animal has its own way of coping. (7) Sea anemones close up into soft blobs to keep from drying out. (8) Barnacles seal their shells shut and wait for the water to return. (9) Tide pools are also very pretty to look at. (10) Sea stars grip the rocks with hundreds of tiny tube feet so the waves cannot wash them away.

(11) Visitors can help protect these animals. (12) They should step only on bare rock and never take animals home. (13) With a little care, tide pools can stay full of life for future visitors to explore.$q$, 'draft')
