insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('24cd62a3-4bca-5e72-ba61-f89a832c31f5', 'wg8-informative-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$How a Mosaic Comes Together$q$, $q$(1) A mosaic is a picture or pattern made from many small pieces of material set close together. (2) The pieces, called tesserae, can be cut from glass, stone, tile, or even shells. (3) Artists have made mosaics for thousands of years, and the basic steps have changed very little.

(4) First, the artist sketches a design on a sturdy base such as wood or cement board. (5) Next, the artist cuts the tesserae into shapes using a tool called a nipper. (6) Then each piece is pressed into a layer of adhesive, leaving a narrow gap between pieces. (7) After the adhesive dries, the artist fills these gaps with grout, a thick paste that hardens like cement. (8) Finally, the surface is wiped clean so the colors show clearly.

(9) Mosaics appear in many places. (10) The city library has a mosaic of a winding river on its front wall. (11) Students at Eastfield Middle School created a mosaic bench using broken tiles donated by families. (12) It was really nice and stuff.$q$, 'draft')
